        row.createdAt.toISOString(),
        row.failureReason ?? "",
      ].map(val => `"${String(val).replace(/"/g, '""')}"`);
```
The csv generating code replaces `"` with `""` but if the string contains a CRLF (`\r\n`), `val` contains new line characters causing the `csv` to break when parsed into an application. Excel requires quotes, which is satisfied here, but `csv` specification (RFC 4180) allows multiline if escaped correctly, but this does work for CSV. 

